## Routing Rules

- For **planning or specifications**, start with `working-principles/references/planning.md` when clarification is needed. Product intent/PRDs → `brainstorming` (settled-direction path); technical constraints/TRDs → `architecture-design`; behavior examples/BDD/acceptance criteria → `code-craft` (specification-only path); journeys/states → `ui-ux`; publication/presentation → `doc-craft`. Use only the needed owner, not an artifact ladder. A specification request grants no implementation authority.
- Prefer no skill for simple edits (formatting, config values, renaming only).
- Prefer the narrowest skill that matches the user intent.
- On non-trivial requests or explicit team-based “work until done” loops, load `team-operating-model` before substantive work and form a real primary-plus-worker team. Use its delivery, deliberation, and persistent paths as needed; unavailable permitted delegation blocks rather than switching to solo/simulation. Trivial work stays outside activation; selection does not grant launch authority. `subagent-dispatch` governs every permitted worker launch.
- Quick/narrow explicit reviews use one primary matching reviewer skill.
- Broad, mixed, or deep explicit reviews load the `reviewer` skill (or use the harness's built-in `/review` command).
- Load deep references only after the selected skill requests them.
- For skill composition patterns and handoff points, see `WIRING`.
- For project setup from scratch: `project-foundation` → `devsecops` (bootstrap foundation first, then harden the pipeline with security).
- For governance maintenance: `skill-author` Workflow B (audit); if gaps found, route to `skill-author` Workflow A (create) or `project-foundation`.
- For **personal/portfolio investment decisions (any asset class)**: `investment-assessment` (author) → optional `team-operating-model` deliberation/finance cast or `reviewer` `investment-memo` lens for high-stakes challenge. Credit/bond is a module under that skill, not a separate default. Finance personas: `team-operating-model/references/personas/finance/`.
- Management reports and metrics: use `docs/ai-augmented-project-setup-and-evolution.md` §9 as a reference for what to report, not a skill workflow. Each org's reporting format varies — define your template and generate ad-hoc.
